book class_reference_arrays_matrix
read everything from nil.std.collections

Counter begin record
    field total as override integer
end record

abstract Reader begin class
    field total as override integer
    public abstract read-total returns override integer
end class

OffsetReader inherits Reader begin class
    field offset as override integer
    public replaces read-total returns override integer begin paragraph
        give my total plus my offset
    end paragraph
end class

read-first receives values as array of Reader returns override integer begin paragraph
    give (values at 0).read-total with nothing
end paragraph

make-readers receives item as OffsetReader returns array of Reader begin paragraph
    give [item]
end paragraph

main returns override integer begin paragraph
    value object is build OffsetReader with total being 7, offset being 2
    value readers as array of Reader is [object]
    value alias is readers
    append object to readers
    set readers at 0 to object
    evaluate readers.set with 1, object
    evaluate readers.reserve with 33
    say (alias at 0).read-total with nothing
    say (alias at 1).read-total with nothing
    say the length of readers
    say (readers.capacity with nothing) is at least 33
    say read-first with values being [object]
    value returned is make-readers with item being object
    say (returned at 0).read-total with nothing
    value filled is new-with-value of Reader with size being 3, `value` being object
    evaluate array-set of Reader with arr being filled, idx being 1, `value` being object
    value selected is get of Reader with arr being filled, idx being 1
    say selected.read-total with nothing
    say try-copy-range of Reader with source being filled, source-offset being 0, destination being filled, destination-offset being 1, count being 2
    value rows as array of array of Reader is [readers, []]
    append object to (rows at 1)
    set ((rows at 1) at 0).total to 17
    say object.read-total with nothing

    value counter-value is build Counter with total being 23
    value refs as array of reference to Counter is [reference to counter-value]
    value retained is refs at 0
    append reference to counter-value to refs
    evaluate refs.reserve with 17
    set (refs at 0).total to 29
    say counter-value.total
    say retained.total
    value other is build Counter with total being 31
    set refs at 0 to reference to other
    say retained.total
    say (refs at 0).total
    value refs-filled is new-with-value of reference to Counter with size being 3, `value` being retained
    evaluate array-set of reference to Counter with arr being refs-filled, idx being 1, `value` being (reference to other)
    value found is get of reference to Counter with arr being refs-filled, idx being 1
    say found.total
    say try-copy-range of reference to Counter with source being refs-filled, source-offset being 0, destination being refs-filled, destination-offset being 1, count being 2
    say (refs-filled at 1).total
    say (refs-filled at 2).total
    value ref-rows as array of array of reference to Counter is [refs, []]
    append retained to (ref-rows at 1)
    set ((ref-rows at 1) at 0).total to 37
    say counter-value.total
    value empty as array of reference to Counter is []
    evaluate empty.reserve with 11
    say the length of empty
    give 0
end paragraph
